bles with your  chopsticks and push them all towards the  front as if you're rolling a carpet oil  it up one more time and add a bit more  eggs make sure to get underneath the  first roll so it kind of glues together  a bit you're gonna have to do this three  more times until it's one large roll at  this point just transfer to a plate and  that's it never seen an omelet this  color but it looks like and it's not  gonna have any flavor to it because  there is no ingredients other than an  egg on it visually it's a no for me this  looks sweet  it likes sparkles the roll is really  perfect look at that roll it doesn't  look like there's anything in it it's  just an egg over and over and over again  I even know what I'm tasting right now I  really like this  there's definitely something sweet about  it I don't think there's enough  happening for me to like it  it's a thumbs down I like this I'm  feeling this half of the food eating  experiences like aesthetics so I dig  this  I love Cool J starts by separating a  whopping nine egg whites from their  yolks he sprays a pan on nonstick spray  adds diced yellow and red peppers and  cooks those until tender you're gonna  want to break up your egg whites just a  little bit so they're not all stuck  together add some spinach to the pan  salt and pepper and let the spinach wilt  so it gets nice and tender add your egg  whites back to the pan and push them  around with your rubber spatula a little  bit to help them cook evenly season  again with salt and pepper and let them  cook up so they set all the way on the  bottom fold it in half into a half moon  shape transfer it on to a plate and  that's it turns out nine egg yolks is  how 50 rolls stays so ripped whoa egg  whites are we healthy or not a lot of  vegetables happening it's important to  get your vitamins I mean its eggs so how  bad could it be  mm-hmm pretty bad yeah it tastes way too  healthy like something my mom is forcing  me to eat the vegetables don't add  anything